/E (HELIX achieved the highest average accuracy \(0.80\) and the lowest forgetting \(0.04\) among the three approaches. Its performance remained relatively stable across developmental stages, while the Static model showed a larger decline as the data distribution changed. HELIX triggered 3 adaptations across 5 stages, indicating that it adapted selectively rather than updating unnecessarily.)
